MQDEsys Commercial Contribution Covenant

Commercial use of the Software, including commercial distribution, hosted
services, paid integration, or a commercial derivative, is permitted only
subject to the following additional covenant:

1. Twenty percent (20%) of the gross commercial revenue attributable to the
   Software must be paid to the official MQDEsys project account or funding
   channel published by the project. The payment must be made within sixty
   (60) calendar days after the revenue is received.
2. Of each payment made under paragraph 1, forty percent (40%) must be
   distributed among all MQDEsys contributors recorded in the project's
   published contribution records. The remaining sixty percent (60%)
   must be retained for MQDEsys maintenance, infrastructure, documentation,
   security, and feature development.
3. A commercial user must keep reasonable records supporting the revenue
   calculation and provide a summary to the project maintainers upon
   reasonable request.

For this covenant, "gross commercial revenue attributable to the Software"
means the revenue received from products, services, hosted access, licenses,
or integrations in which the Software or a derivative of it is a material
component, before deduction of operating costs. This covenant is a material
condition of the license for commercial use. It does not limit non-commercial
use permitted by the MIT terms above.

